# Port of pi-ux 0.6.6 into the ceulen ux module:
# - hooks/ux-audit.js  → lib/audit.ts (CJS → ESM TS, logic verbatim)
# - hooks/ux-config.js → lib/config.ts (getHideStatus dropped — no status bar)
# - hooks/ux-instructions.js → lib/instructions.ts (SKILL.md path → package skills/)
# - extensions/index.js → index.ts
# - skills/ux-{design,capture,presets,routing} → package skills/ (upstream content)
#
# Deliberate divergences from upstream:
# - NO status bar: no setStatus, no agent_start/agent_end sync, no hideStatus
#   setting/env (PI_UX_HIDE_STATUS is ignored).
# - Bare /ux reports status instead of resetting to the default (ponytail #99
#   precedent, same as ceulen's ponytail module).
# - /ux default <mode> subcommand dropped — the default mode is owned by the
#   central /config panel (ux.defaultMode row) writing via writeDefaultMode.
# - parseUxCommand/parse API mirrors ceulen's ponytail (status/set-mode/invalid).
#
# Config contract preserved from upstream: ~/.config/pi-ux/config.json
# (defaultMode, quietStartup) + PI_UX_DEFAULT_MODE / PI_UX_QUIET_STARTUP env
# overrides — existing pi-ux users keep their settings across the port.
